HOW TO USE,,,,,,,,,,
"1. Open the class tab (1-A, 1-B …). Each student has one row; each day of the month has one column.",,,,,,,,,,
2. Absent → type A.   Leave permission → type L.   Present → type P.  (small letters a / l / p also work.),,,,,,,,,,
"3. A = red cell, L = yellow cell, P = green cell. Friday and Saturday columns are light grey (weekend). Days before school started (1–19 September 2026) are dark grey and not counted.",,,,,,,,,,
"4. At the end of every month there are three count columns, A, L and P, per student, and class totals under the last student. They are automatic — do not type in them.",,,,,,,,,,
"5. The last two columns of each class tab give the whole-year totals for A, L and P.",,,,,,,,,,
,,,,,,,,,,
REPORT TABS,,,,,,,,,,
"Class Summary — absences (A) and leave permissions (L) for every class, month by month (present days P are counted on each class tab).",,,,,,,,,,
"Student Report — every student with A and L per month and for the year. Use the filter arrows (e.g. Total A greater than 0, or a class) to build a list.",,,,,,,,,,
Top Absentees — the 15 students with the most absences so far (updates itself).,,,,,,,,,,
